'' '#cmdline' INJECTS ITS ARGUMENTS INTO THE COMPILE THAT READ IT, which tiko does
'' the way fbc does: by running the whole compile again with them appended. This is
'' fbc's own test for the directive (tests/vendor/fbc-tests/pp/cmdline.bas) in tiko's
'' harness, '-restart' and all -- fbc needs telling to restart, tiko always does, and
'' a source that says so must not become an unknown-option error.
''
'' A FAILURE HERE IS AN EXIT OF 1, not a wrong number: without the restart
'' CMDLINESYMBOL is undefined and the '#error' below is what the run reports.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --parse-only %s
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0

#cmdline "-d CMDLINESYMBOL"
#cmdline "-restart"

#if not defined( CMDLINESYMBOL )
#error the restart did not happen
#endif

print "ok"
